---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy">
  <div class="page">
    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">04 / Privacy</p><h1>Privacy</h1></div></div>
      <div class="empty">
        <p>The public Library is static-first and uses no behavioral analytics in the v1 architecture. Reading state, saved works, offline state, annotations, backup/restore state, and personal book imports are designed to remain in the browser.</p>
        <p>When you import an EPUB or PDF into My Library, the file is inspected and stored in this browser’s local IndexedDB storage. Thiepn Library does not upload the personal book to a server. EPUB metadata and covers are read locally for display in My Library; personal EPUB/PDF reading also occurs from the locally stored file.</p>
        <p>Manual JSON backups contain reading state and personal-book identity/metadata, but they do not contain personal EPUB/PDF file bytes. Re-importing the matching file reconnects it by its SHA-256 content identity. Backup is manual portability, not account or cloud synchronization.</p>
        <p>The interface currently loads its webfont styles/fonts from Google Fonts. That causes ordinary font-resource requests to Google’s font infrastructure and may expose normal network information such as your IP address and browser request metadata to that provider. The Library does not use those requests for behavioral analytics.</p>
        <p>Clearing browser site data can remove locally imported books and reading state. Browser storage may also be subject to device storage policies. Use <a href="../backup">Backup &amp; restore</a> if you want a portable copy of supported reading state.</p>
        <p>The optional Ask Library service is separate from the public application and must be owner-authenticated before provider work occurs.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
